# Next.js / React UI

## App structure

- App Router only (`src/app`). No Pages Router.
- Use `'use client'` when the file needs state, effects, or browser APIs (see `@src/app/components/app-shell.tsx`, `@src/app/components/ui/navbar.tsx`, `@src/app/components/terminal/fullscreen-terminal.tsx`).
- Put new UI under `src/app/components/ui/` (or `src/app/components/terminal/` for the assistant overlay) unless introducing a clearer feature folder by request.
- Global shell lives in `@src/app/layout.tsx` → `@src/app/components/app-shell.tsx`: `ChatProvider` wraps every route, plus `ThemeBackground`, `Navbar`, and `LazyOverlays` (the terminal chunk loads only after first open). Add new global overlays there, not in `page.tsx`. Do not reintroduce a global footer with duplicate contact/social links — those live in `ContactSection`.
- Home page (`@src/app/page.tsx`) composition: `Hero` → `ExperienceTimeline` (`#experience`; each role's Details expands to highlights plus compact work-project summaries that link to `/projects/<slug>`) → `ProjectsSection` (`#projects`, personal projects only — compact two-column grid of equal-height entries with a clamped description, capped tech list, and no inline metrics; metrics and the full case study live on `/projects/<slug>`) → `SkillsGrid` (`#skills`) → `AboutSection` (`#about`, bio plus quiet chat entry) → `OutsideWork` → `ContactSection` (`#contact`).
- Project detail pages: `@src/app/projects/[slug]/page.tsx`, server-rendered from `@src/shared/projects.ts` with `generateStaticParams` + `generateMetadata` for every project. Work projects (`origin: 'work'`) still list under the owning role in `ExperienceTimeline` via `getProjectsByExperienceId`; their case studies live at `/projects/<slug>` (back link to `/#experience`). Personal projects list in `ProjectsSection` and use the same route (back link to `/#projects`).
- Backend Route Handlers live under `src/app/api/v1/` (not in the UI tree); keep secrets and LLM/DB work out of client components.

## Styling

- Tailwind + existing shadcn primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Card`, `ScrollArea`).
- Merge classes with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` (`@src/lib/utils.ts`).
- Use themeable `surface-*` / `glow` tokens (`bg-surface-950` page, hairline `border-surface-800/70` dividers, sage `glow` accent). Never hardcode `zinc-*` or raw hex.
- Editorial layout: sections are typography-first (serif `font-display` headings, mono eyebrows) separated by whitespace and hairlines — do not wrap sections in bordered card containers. Cards/containment are reserved for the terminal overlay.
- Single dark look: `html.dark` plus `surface-*` / `glow` tokens in `@src/app/globals.css`. Ambient background is `@src/app/components/ui/theme-background.tsx`. Do not add album theme switching unless requested.
- Mono UI (terminal, tech lists, metadata) uses `font-mono` → JetBrains Mono via `--font-mono`; body is Geist and headings are Instrument Serif via `--font-display`.
- Use `ScrollArea` for dark-themed scroll regions; keep `color-scheme: dark` on `html`.
- Skill logos come from `@src/shared/skillIcons.ts` (inline path data) if icons are reintroduced; the skills section currently renders grouped typography without icons. Never `import { … } from 'simple-icons'` — the package barrel is multi-MB and stalls SSR/dev compiles.
- `components.json` may alias utils to `@/app/lib/utils`; the real file is `@/lib/utils`. Do not duplicate `utils.ts` to “fix” the alias.
- Interactive targets should be at least 44px tall (chips, mobile menu buttons, terminal controls) for touch accessibility.

## State and exports

- Prefer local `useState` / `useRef` / `useEffect`. One cross-cutting context exists: `ChatProvider` (`@src/app/components/ui/chat-provider.tsx`). Don't add another global store unless justified.
- Chat thread and overlay open state live in `@src/hooks/useChatThread.ts` and are shared via `useChat()` so any section or Ask Daniel button can call `sendMessage` / `openChat`.
- Match surrounding export style (named for hooks/primitives; default where the file already defaults; `fullscreen-terminal.tsx` default-exports for `next/dynamic`).

## Assistant terminal

Canonical UI: `@src/app/components/terminal/fullscreen-terminal.tsx` (centered modal over a dimmed backdrop). State/streaming: `@src/hooks/useChatThread.ts`.

- Navbar TerminalSquare, Ask Daniel buttons, and the about-section CTA all call `openChat({ context? })`
- Transcript is a REPL: user turns as `$ <question>`, assistant turns as streamed markdown
- Render assistant markdown with `react-markdown` + `remark-gfm`
- Stream by appending content chunks to the last assistant message
- Thread with `parent_id` / server `assistant_message_id`
- `useChat()` exposes `openChat({ context, prompt })` / `closeChat()` / `isOpen` / `context` (`{ type: 'project' | 'experience'; id }` or `null`), `error` + `retry()` for a failed send, and `clearChat()`
- Esc and backdrop click close the modal; Ctrl/Cmd+K clears the thread via `@src/hooks/refreshChatKeyHandler.ts`; the title bar also has `[ CLEAR ]` and `[ EXIT ]`
- Autoscroll the transcript container (`scrollTop`), not the whole page (`scrollIntoView`)
- Contextual suggested prompts: general → `CHAT_SUGGESTIONS`, project → `getProjectSuggestions()`, experience → `getExperienceSuggestions()` (both in `@src/shared/`)
- Assistant replies may end with `[[LINK:project:<slug>]]` / `[[LINK:experience:<id>]]` markers (see `@src/lib/sourceLinks.ts`, mirrors `@src/lib/contactCta.ts`); render as clickable chips, never show the raw marker. Chip hrefs: projects link to `/projects/<slug>`, experience ids link to `/#experience`. Source-link clicks close the overlay so the destination is visible.
- Do not call Telegram (or other side-effect notify APIs) after stream completion
- Do not reintroduce a command registry, tokenizer/parser, sidebar chat panel, or inline hero terminal

## Profile content

- Client-facing copy, experience, skills, interests, nav links: `@src/shared/profile.ts`
- Project case studies: `@src/shared/projects.ts` (`PROJECTS`, `PERSONAL_PROJECTS`, `getProjectBySlug`, `getProjectsByExperienceId`); `origin: 'work'` projects need `relatedExperienceId` so they render under the right role in the experience timeline
- Project images live at `public/images/projects/<slug>.png` (or `.webp`, 16:9 ≈1600×900) and are wired through the optional `visual` field in `projects.ts` — `ProjectsSection` shows a 16:9 thumbnail, the detail page shows it large; never hotlink external images
- LLM background facts: `@src/server/ai/systemPrompt.ts` (the bot is Daniel's assistant; speak about him in the third person) — interpolates dates/roles/tech/impact from `profile.ts`/`projects.ts` via `@src/server/ai/context.ts` rather than duplicating them
- When updating jobs/education/location/projects, update `profile.ts`/`projects.ts` first; `systemPrompt.ts` picks up shared facts automatically, but review its hand-written narrative bullets too

## Resume

- Resume is a static asset at `/resume.pdf` (contact section). Do not add a custom resume API route unless requested.
